#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Time-of-use tariffs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"With a time-variable (dynamic) electricity tariff, the price changes over "
"the day, usually every quarter of an hour, linked to the exchange "
"electricity price. OpenEMS can align the storage accordingly: **avoid "
"expensive grid power, use cheap power**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What OpenEMS does"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-openems-does
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"**Save the storage for expensive hours:** In cheap hours, the power comes "
"from the grid and the storage is conserved. In expensive hours, the storage "
"supplies the house."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-openems-does
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"**Charge from the grid** (optional): In particularly cheap hours, the "
"storage is charged from the grid to bridge expensive hours later."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-openems-does
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"**Sell to the grid** (optional): In particularly expensive hours, the "
"storage can discharge into the grid."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-openems-does
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"**Comply with limits:** The maximum grid purchase power and the feed-in "
"limit of the system are always taken into account."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-openems-does
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"Charging from the grid is only worthwhile if the price difference is large "
"enough. Energy is lost during charging and discharging, and OpenEMS takes "
"this into account. It therefore rates power that takes the detour via the "
"storage as around 17 % more expensive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where the prices come from"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-where-the-prices-come-from
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"There are three sources for exchange prices (day-ahead). They can be set up "
"at the same time:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Source\n"
"| Priority\n"
"| Notes\n"
"\n"
"| OpenEMS backend\n"
"| 1\n"
"| requires a connection to the backend\n"
"| SMARD (German Federal Network Agency)\n"
"| 2\n"
"| freely usable, only for Germany, Austria, Belgium, the Netherlands and the Czech Republic\n"
"| ENTSO-E\n"
"| 3\n"
"| Europe-wide, requires your own free access key (token)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"A price source is set up via the app **“Spot Tariff Vendor”** (backend, "
"ENTSO-E or SMARD); the tariff apps require it. Older ENTSO-E components are "
"converted automatically. The former setting “Maximum grid purchase through "
"storage charging” no longer exists; the grid purchase limit from the system "
"settings applies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS takes the prices from the source with the highest priority. **If "
"values are missing there, it fills the gaps with the next source**. All "
"prices are converted into the currency stored in the system settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition to exchange prices, there are ready-made connections to "
"individual electricity providers, e.g. Tibber, aWATTar, Rabot Charge, "
"Corrently, Octopus, Groupe E, Swisspower, LUOX or Stadtwerke Haßfurt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the exchange price to your own electricity price"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-the-exchange-price-to-your-own-electricity-price
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"The exchange price is not the price you actually pay. The following are "
"therefore specified for purchase:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-the-exchange-price-to-your-own-electricity-price
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "the **bidding zone** (e.g. Germany/Luxembourg),"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-the-exchange-price-to-your-own-electricity-price
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"the **additional costs** such as grid fees, taxes and levies, also staggered "
"by time of day,"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-the-exchange-price-to-your-own-electricity-price
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"optionally a **formula** for how the exchange price and additional costs are "
"offset. Default: exchange price {plus} additional costs."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-from-the-exchange-price-to-your-own-electricity-price
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"For feed-in, an exchange price or a fixed remuneration (e.g. according to "
"the German EEG) can also be stored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up price control"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setting-up-price-control
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "The function is called **Controller.Ess.Time-Of-Use-Tariff**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operating mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-operating-mode
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "**Automatic** (default): OpenEMS plans by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-operating-mode
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "**Manual:** A permanently selected behavior is applied continuously."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-operating-mode
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"**Off:** normal self-consumption optimization without reference to prices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How far control may go"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Permitted behavior\n"
"\n"
"| Delay discharge (default)\n"
"| Save the storage for expensive hours\n"
"| Charge from grid\n"
"| additionally charge from the grid in cheap hours\n"
"| Discharge to grid\n"
"| additionally sell to the grid in expensive hours\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The states you see"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| State\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Self-consumption optimization\n"
"| normal operation: charge surplus, cover demand from the storage\n"
"| Delayed discharge\n"
"| Storage is conserved for more expensive times, the house draws grid power\n"
"| Charge from grid\n"
"| Storage is charged at a low price\n"
"| Discharge to grid\n"
"| Storage sells power at a high price\n"
"| Peak shaving\n"
"| Storage helps not to exceed the maximum grid purchase power\n"
"| Avoid feed-in limit\n"
"| Storage absorbs surplus so that the feed-in limit is complied with\n"
"| Delayed / limited charging, discharge for consumption\n"
"| only together with xref:user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc[grid-optimized charge]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"“Peak shaving” and “Avoid feed-in limit” are not planned. They occur at "
"short notice if the planned state would otherwise violate a limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How OpenEMS plans"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"For the next few hours, an optimizer tries out many possible sequences: "
"which state should apply when. It calculates each sequence with the "
"xref:user/schedule/forecasts.adoc[forecasts] for solar yield and consumption "
"and with the electricity prices. It selects the sequence that performs best "
"in this order:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "All limits are complied with and consumption is covered."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "**Electricity costs** are as low as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "Grid purchase is as low as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "Feed-in revenues are as high as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid "There are as few changes between states as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-openems-plans
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"The plan is renewed regularly (about every quarter of an hour) so that new "
"prices and more accurate forecasts are included. The result is the xref:user/"
"schedule/overview.adoc[schedule]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"The plan is only as good as the forecasts. If the day differs greatly (e.g. "
"unexpectedly high consumption), it may in hindsight not have been optimal."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"Without prices, for example if no source can be reached, price-optimized "
"planning is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"With price control in “Automatic” mode, the optimizer also takes over the "
"task of grid-optimized charge."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"The optimizer does not plan for a xref:user/storage-control/section-14a-"
"enwg.adoc[§ 14a limitation] of the storage (maximum 4.2 kW charging power). "
"It is nevertheless complied with during operation: during an intervention, "
"the storage charges correspondingly less than planned."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc
msgid ""
"The level of a xref:user/storage-control/ripple-control-receiver.adoc[ripple "
"control receiver] (0/30/60 %) is **not** taken into account by price "
"control, neither in the schedule nor during operation. Only the feed-in "
"limit from the system settings is taken into account. The inverter still "
"complies with the ripple control limitation. During a limitation, however, "
"PV power may be curtailed even though the storage could have absorbed it."
msgstr ""
